{"availability":"available","full":"alexberriman/rulebridge","name":"rulebridge","description":"Convert rules between json-rules-engine, JsonLogic, json-logic-engine, filtrex, jexl, expr-eval, expression-eval and Casbin matchers. Any-to-any through one canonical IR, Rust-style Result API, zero runtime dependencies.","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":12,"forks":2,"created":"2022-07-05T06:26:56Z","updated":"2026-09-19T10:14:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alexberriman.github.io/rulebridge/","topics":["business-rules","casbin","converter","dsl","expr-eval","expression-eval","filtrex","interoperability","jexl","json-logic","json-logic-js","json-rules-engine","jsonlogic","rule-engine","rules","rules-engine","serialization","typescript","zero-dependencies"],"demo":"https://alexberriman.github.io/rulebridge/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.446Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.446Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.446Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.446Z","stars":12,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One rule, every engine. Convert rules between json-rules-engine, JsonLogic, json-logic-engine, filtrex, jexl, expr-eval, expression-eval and Casbin matchers.","There are several popular, serializable rule formats in the JS ecosystem, and they do not interoperate. A condition written for json-rules-engine cannot be fed to a service that speaks JsonLogic. A filtrex filter expression cannot be stored next to a jexl policy. You pick one engine and you are locked in.","rulebridge is a portability layer. It converts a rule from any supported format into any other, through a single canonical intermediate representation (IR). Migrate off a rules engine, feed rules built for one library into another, or store rules in a neutral shape. rulebridge does the translation, and it tells you, precisely and structurally, when something cannot be translated."],"features":["Any-to-any conversion between 8 popular formats through one canonical IR (N codecs, not N-squared pairwise converters).","Rust-style Result API. Conversions return Result instead of throwing. Errors are structured data (code, message, path, format), never exceptions.","Zero runtime dependencies and zero type-only dependencies. The published types reference nothing external.","Honest about loss. Every format has different expressiveness. rulebridge never silently produces a wrong rule: untranslatable constructs return a typed Err, and the fidelity tiers are documented up front.","Cross-format equivalence is verified by converting rules and evaluating them in each format's native engine."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexberriman/rulebridge/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"06970a168ec4aa9c188adcc1a5aa1c55e2037327496fffdd1a5e8dc057e4cd63","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.523Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.523Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"One rule, every engine. Convert rules between json-rules-engine, JsonLogic, json-logic-engine, filtrex, jexl, expr-eval, expression-eval and Casbin matchers.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexberriman/rulebridge/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"rulebridge is a portability layer. It converts a rule from any supported format into any other, through a single canonical intermediate representation (IR). Migrate off a rules engine, feed rules built for one library into another, or store rules in a neutral shape. rulebridge does the translation, and it tells you, precisely and structurally, when something cannot be…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexberriman/rulebridge/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"06970a168ec4aa9c188adcc1a5aa1c55e2037327496fffdd1a5e8dc057e4cd63","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexberriman/rulebridge/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:47.523Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-19T10:14:56Z","